{"shortDescription":"The euro traded just below $1.15, near its weakest level since late July, and was down nearly 1% against the US dollar as traders scaled back expectations for further ECB rate hikes.The pullback came despite a more restrictive tone from the Federal Reserve, which raised rates this week and signaled…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The euro traded just below $1.15, near its weakest level since late July, and was down nearly 1% against the US dollar as traders scaled back expectations for further ECB rate hikes."]},{"type":"p","children":["The pullback came despite a more restrictive tone from the Federal Reserve, which raised rates this week and signaled scope for further tightening, following a similar move by the ECB last week."]},{"type":"p","children":["Some analysts argued that markets had gone too far in pricing additional ECB hikes, noting that higher energy prices could weigh on growth and ultimately ease inflationary pressures."]},{"type":"p","children":["Money markets now price the ECB deposit rate at just below 2.9% by December, implying roughly a 50% chance of a second hike this year."]},{"type":"p","children":["By November 2027, rates are priced at 3.39%."]},{"type":"p","children":["Elsewhere, the Bank of England held rates steady on Thursday but warned that a prolonged Middle East conflict could prompt tighter policy, while the Bank of Japan raised rates to their highest level in 31 years and signaled further tightening ahead."]}]},"language":"en","tags":[{"title":"Forex","args":[{"id":"category","value":"forex"}]},{"title":"Trading Economics","args":[{"id":"provider","value":"trading-economics"}]}],"id":"te_news:584964:0","title":"Euro Nears July Low as Markets Scale Back ECB Rate-Hike Bets","published":1789719299,"urgency":2,"link":"https://tradingeconomics.com/euro-area/currency","permission":"preview","relatedSymbols":[{"symbol":"FX:EURUSD","currency-logoid":"country/US","base-currency-logoi